{"chunk_id": "275de2b7b8a7", "text": "This section connects the story of King Swetaki\u2019s immense sacrifice to the famous burning of the Khandava forest. After Swetaki completes a twelve\u2011year sacrifice assisted by the sage Durvasa, Agni (the fire god) becomes ill from consuming an endless stream of clarified butter offered in the ritual. Weak and unable to shine, Agni seeks help from Brahma, who advises him that only by devouring the creatures of the vast Khandava forest can he restore his strength. Agni repeatedly attempts to burn the forest but its inhabitants\u2014elephants, serpents, and other creatures\u2014extinguish the flames. Frustrated, he again consults Brahma, who directs him to seek the aid of the incarnate heroes Nara and Narayana, now living as Arjuna and Krishna, setting the stage for the legendary Khandava forest conflagration.\nSwetaki completes his sacrifice with Durvasa\u2019s help; Agni, sick from excess ghee, is advised by Brahma to burn Khandava with aid from Krishna and Arjuna.\nThemes: sacrifice and ritual excess, divine intervention, Agni's illness, Khandava forest, Krishna and Arjuna as incarnations", "vector": [0.016825959086418152, -0.015081553719937801, -0.010576317086815834, 0.012842671014368534, -0.012437473982572556, 0.026289701461791992, -0.024325529113411903, -0.008948663249611855, -0.019861498847603798, -0.005562867969274521, 0.004316373728215694, 0.012341326102614403, 0.02321295626461506, 0.006864304654300213, -0.006115721073001623, -0.003876838367432356, 0.04834887757897377, 0.0015735705383121967, 0.023377781733870506, -0.018240712583065033, -0.02462770976126194, 0.005013449117541313, -0.00927831418812275, 0.026111140847206116, 0.0001767369540175423, 0.01773250102996826, 0.012897612527012825, -0.021427342668175697, 0.008316830731928349, 0.0034802264999598265, -0.00816574040800333, -0.016043037176132202, -0.00010414281132398173, -0.001041320851072669, -0.014600811526179314, -0.008543466217815876, -0.018474215641617775, -0